{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":75613316,"ns":0,"title":"Rouben Azizian","revisions":[{"revid":1380332315,"parentid":1375058817,"minor":true,"timestamp":"2026-10-15T02:47:31Z","size":7163,"sha1":"7c8ea0efe98dd4bf2438c3a6036e64e9fff1cf4d","slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","content":"{{Short description|New Zealand political scientist}}\n\n{{Third-party|date=December 2023}}\n{{Infobox academic\n| name              = Rouben Azizian\n| native_name       = \n| native_name_lang  = \n| image             = \n| image_size        = \n| alt               = \n| caption           = \n| birth_name        = \n| birth_date        = {{Birth date and age|1950|03|25}}\n| birth_place       = \n| citizenship       = \n| discipline        = [[Political science|Political scientist]]\n| sub_discipline    = [[Security studies]], [[International relations]]\n| institutions      = [[Massey University]]\n| patrons           = \n| education         = [[Diplomatic Academy of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Russian Federation|Diplomatic Academy of the USSR MFA]]\n| thesis1_title     = \n| thesis1_url       = \n| thesis1_year      = \n| doctoral_advisor  = \n| academic_advisors = \n| doctoral_students = \n| notable_students  = \n| known_for         = \n| author_abbrev_bot = \n| author_abbrev_zoo = \n| influences        = \n| influenced        = \n| awards            = \n| signature         = <!--(filename only)-->\n| signature_alt     = \n| website           = <!-- {{URL|www.example.com}} -->\n| footnotes         = \n| spouse            = \n| children          = \n}}\n\n'''Rouben Azizian''' is a New Zealand academic of Armenian descent. He specialises in [[security studies]] and [[international relations]] in the [[Asia–Pacific]]. He is currently a full professor at [[Massey University]] and head of the Auckland branch of the New Zealand Institute of International Affairs.\n\n== Biography ==\nAzizian acquired a Master of Arts degree at the [[Moscow State Institute of International Relations]] in 1972 and a PhD at the [[Diplomatic Academy of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Russian Federation|Diplomatic Academy of the USSR MFA]] in 1987.{{cn|date=December 2023}}\n\nPrior to becoming a full-time academic, Azizian worked as a [[USSR|Soviet]] (and later, [[Russia]]n) diplomat. He was assigned to the missions in [[Nepal]] and [[Sri Lanka]] before he came to [[New Zealand]] in 1991 as a counsellor and deputy chief of mission at the Soviet embassy in [[Wellington]]. He quit his diplomatic career in 1994 but stayed in the country and started teaching at the Department of Political Studies at the [[University of Auckland]].<ref>{{cite web|title = Prof Rouben Azizian, PhD|url = https://www.massey.ac.nz/massey/expertise/profile.cfm?stref=318350|website = Massey University|access-date = 21 December 2023}}</ref>\n\nBetween 2002 and 2015, Azizian lectured and conducted research at the [[Asia-Pacific Center for Security Studies]] in [[Honolulu]]. He then returned to his New Zealand home to become the Director of Massey University's Centre for Defence and Security Studies.<ref>{{cite web|title = Dr. Rouben Azizian departs DKI APCSS for New Zealand university leadership role|date = 8 January 2016|website = [[Asia-Pacific Center for Security Studies]]|url = https://dkiapcss.edu/dr-rouben-azizian-departs-dki-apcss-for-new-zealand-university-leadership-role/|access-date = 21 December 2023}}</ref> In 2019, he became the founding editor of New Zealand's first scholarly journal in his field, the ''National Security Journal''.<ref>{{cite journal|last1 = Azizian|first1 = Rouben|date = 2019|title = Welcome to the National Security Journal|url = https://sites.massey.ac.nz/wp-content/uploads/sites/13/2019/09/NSJ-2019-October-Azizian.pdf|journal = National Security Journal|volume = 1|issue = 1|pages = 1–4}}</ref>\n\nIn addition to his academic work, Azizian has appeared on numerous podcasts and interviews as an international relations commentator and foreign policy educator.<ref>{{cite web|title = The Service: The State, Secrets and Spies|date = 2020|website = [[Radio New Zealand]]|url = https://shorthand.radionz.co.nz/the-service-podcast/index.html|access-date = 21 December 2023}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|title = Russians are trying to flee the country following Vladimir Putin's comments|date = 2023|website = Newstalk ZB|url = https://www.newstalkzb.co.nz/on-air/heather-du-plessis-allan-drive/audio/rouben-azizian-director-for-the-centre-for-defence-and-security-studies-at-massey-university-on-russia/|access-date = 21 December 2022}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|last = Weekes|first = John|title = Russia-Ukraine war: Kiwis could help 'strategic breakthrough' in fightback against Putin|date = 2022|website = [[The New Zealand Herald]]|url = https://www.nzherald.co.nz/nz/russia-ukraine-war-kiwis-could-help-strategic-breakthrough-in-fightback-against-putin/UN75OYUO7RUED7UNOYRI27UEK4/|accessdate = 21 December 2023}}</ref>\n\n==Selected works==\n*{{cite journal|last1 = Azizian|first1 = Rouben|date = 2003|title = A Marriage of Convenience: Russia and U.S. Foreign Policy|url = https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/abs/10.1080/00927670309601525|journal = Asian Affairs: An American Review|volume = 30|issue = 2|pages = 151–159| doi=10.1080/00927670309601525 | s2cid=154211885 |url-access = subscription}}\n*{{cite book|last1 = Azizian|first1 = Rouben|date = 2006|editor-last1 = Aldis|editor-first1 = Anne|editor-last2 = Herd|editor-first2 = Graeme|title = The Ideological War on Terror: Worldwide Strategies for Counter-Terrorism|publisher = Routledge|pages = 81–95|chapter = Islamic Radicalism in Kazakhstan and Kyrgyzstan| doi=10.4324/9780203968420 | isbn=978-0-203-96842-0 |chapter-url = https://www.taylorfrancis.com/chapters/edit/10.4324/9780203968420-8/islamic-radicalism-kazakhstan-kyrgyzstan-rouben-azizian}}\n*{{cite book|last1 = Azizian|first1 = Rouben|date = 2006|editor-last1 = Patman|editor-first1 = Robert|title = Globalization and Conflict: National Security in a 'New' Strategic Era|publisher = Routledge|pages = 135–150|chapter = Russia, America and New Conflicts in Central Asia| doi=10.4324/9780203007938 | isbn=978-0-203-00793-8 |chapter-url = https://www.taylorfrancis.com/chapters/edit/10.4324/9780203007938-11/russia-america-new-conflicts-central-asia-rouben-azizian}}\n*{{cite journal|last1 = Azizian|first1 = Rouben|last2 = Bainazarova|first2 = Elnara|date = 2012|title = Eurasian Response to China's Rise: Russia and Kazakhstan in Search of Optimal China Policy|url = https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/j.1943-0787.2012.01348.x|journal = [[Asian Politics & Policy]]|volume = 4|issue = 3|pages = 377–399| doi=10.1111/j.1943-0787.2012.01348.x |url-access = subscription}}\n*{{cite book|last1 = Azizian|first1 = Rouben|last2 = Johanson|first2 = Terry|date = 2020|editor-last1 = Weinberg|editor-first1 = Leonard|editor-last2 = Francis|editor-first2 = Elizabeth|editor-last3 = Assoudeh|editor-first3 = Eliot|title = Routledge Handbook of Democracy and Security|publisher = Routledge|chapter = Finding the Democratic Balance: Australian and New Zealand National Security Coordination|url = https://www.routledge.com/Routledge-Handbook-of-Democracy-and-Security/Weinberg-Francis-Assoudeh/p/book/9781138799981}}\n\n==References==\n{{reflist}}\n\n{{Authority control}}\n\n{{DEFAULTSORT:Azizian, Rouben}}\n[[Category:Academic staff of Massey University]]\n[[Category:New Zealand political scientists]]\n[[Category:1950 births]]\n[[Category:Living people]]"}}}],"contentmodel":"wikitext","pagelanguage":"en","pagelanguagehtmlcode":"en","pagelanguagedir":"ltr","touched":"2026-11-17T20:09:40Z","lastrevid":1380332315,"length":7163}]}}